<!--
  RM_Thurrock.xml                                GREENTIDE_THURROCK_HERD_BUILD_1

  The thurrock: a giant tree-felling browser that moves in herds. The item is the authority
  (infrastructure/state/items/GREENTIDE_THURROCK_HERD_BUILD_1.md). Everything here reuses built work:

  - The felling is the built Shatterer aura, HediffComp_PeriodicAreaAttack with
    fellsTreesBelowHealthFraction (mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards). A tree beaten low enough falls
    through RM_TreeFallUtility.FellTree (FallCause.Shattered) and drops its wood, the same path the
    crack fall uses. This is the aura's first creature carrier.
  - "Always has the hediff from spawn" was ALREADY BUILT, despite the item saying no such wiring exists:
    RM_CompGrantHediff / CompProperties_GrantHediff (mandrake.rm.creaturebehaviors,
    ROT_WOUND_SHARING_WIRING_1). It adds the hediff in PostSpawnSetup only if missing, so a save/load
    round trip leaves exactly one. No new innate-hediff comp was written.
  - Provoked wall damage (§6): the one new piece is RM_HediffComp_AggroSeverity (creaturebehaviors),
    which holds severity 0.5 at rest and 1.0 while Pawn.InAggroMentalState. A second aura comp with
    minSeverity 0.9 hits buildings only (natural rock spared), so a calm thurrock never damages a building.
  - Rut brawls (§5): DROPPED. RimSage (decompiled 1.6, 2026-10-06) has no rut field or rut-fight
    behaviour on RaceProperties or anywhere in the source; per the item, no new AI is written for it.
  - No moult, no shed: nothing of the kind exists on these defs (the moult is not built).
  - No RM_SilenceAuraExtension (§7): it is not a hunter.
  - Mod Settings (§9): Greentide settings -> RM_ThurrockAuraApplier writes them onto these comps' live props.

  Every number below marked PROVISIONAL is an invented first value, not a measurement.
  Aura tuning target (§4): a herd of 3-6 fells "a handful of trees per in-game hour". At 25 Blunt every
  250 ticks (10 bursts/hour) a 300 HP Greentide tree drops below 40% after ~8 bursts, so a thurrock
  lingering by a tree fells it in under an hour. PROVISIONAL; the felling-pace slider scales the interval.

  Art: generated, not yet installed. artpipe_state.py find thurrock (2026-10-06) -> done/RM_Thurrock_{south,
  east,north} and _artsrc/RM_Thurrock_{south,east,north}/ (art list
  infrastructure/artpipe/art_lists/greentide_turn1_2026-10-02.csv, drawSize 4.5). The texPath below is
  where the art ledger's install must land it.
-->
<Defs>

  <HediffDef>
    <defName>RM_ThurrockShatter</defName>
    <label>canopy-breaker</label>
    <description>The thurrock's way of life. It leans its whole weight into the trees around it as it browses, and anything green within a few strides takes the blows; a tree beaten low enough comes down across the jungle floor. When it is provoked it shoulders walls and doors the same way. Natural rock it leaves alone.</description>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <everCurableByItem>false</everCurableByItem>
    <scenarioCanAdd>false</scenarioCanAdd>
    <initialSeverity>0.5</initialSeverity>
    <maxSeverity>1</maxSeverity>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>browsing</label>
      </li>
      <li>
        <minSeverity>0.9</minSeverity>
        <label>provoked</label>
      </li>
    </stages>
    <comps>
      <!-- Severity 0.5 at rest, 1.0 while in an aggro mental state (manhunter). -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_HediffCompProperties_AggroSeverity">
        <restSeverity>0.5</restSeverity>
        <aggroSeverity>1</aggroSeverity>
      </li>
      <!-- At rest: trees and plants only. PROVISIONAL numbers (header). -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.HediffCompProperties_PeriodicAreaAttack">
        <radius>2.9</radius>
        <tickIntervalTicks>250</tickIntervalTicks>
        <damageDef>Blunt</damageDef>
        <damageAmount>25</damageAmount>
        <pawnMultiplier>0</pawnMultiplier>
        <buildingMultiplier>0</buildingMultiplier>
        <plantMultiplier>1</plantMultiplier>
        <itemMultiplier>0</itemMultiplier>
        <sparedNaturalRock>true</sparedNaturalRock>
        <sparesCarrier>true</sparesCarrier>
        <requiresAwake>true</requiresAwake>
        <fellsTreesBelowHealthFraction>0.4</fellsTreesBelowHealthFraction>
      </li>
      <!-- Provoked only (minSeverity 0.9): buildings only, natural rock spared. PROVISIONAL numbers. Secondary class: the engine rejects two comps of one compClass. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.HediffCompProperties_PeriodicAreaAttackSecondary">
        <radius>1.9</radius>
        <tickIntervalTicks>60</tickIntervalTicks>
        <damageDef>Blunt</damageDef>
        <damageAmount>30</damageAmount>
        <minSeverity>0.9</minSeverity>
        <pawnMultiplier>0</pawnMultiplier>
        <buildingMultiplier>1</buildingMultiplier>
        <plantMultiplier>0</plantMultiplier>
        <itemMultiplier>0</itemMultiplier>
        <sparedNaturalRock>true</sparedNaturalRock>
        <sparesCarrier>true</sparesCarrier>
        <requiresAwake>true</requiresAwake>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </HediffDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Thurrock</defName>
    <label>thurrock</label>
    <description>A browser the size of a house, humped high over the shoulders and set on four columnar legs caked to the knee in churnmud. Its hide is a wet copper and teal, crusted pale with mineral bloom along the back, and torn leaves ride in its folds wherever it has pushed through the crowns. A short, curling trunk-lip strips a tree bare in a few pulls. Thurrock browse by leaning their whole weight into the trees they feed on, and where a herd has passed, trunks lie across the causeways and light comes down through new holes in the canopy. You hear them long before you see them. They cannot be tamed, and a provoked thurrock shoulders a wall the way it shoulders a tree.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>3.6</MoveSpeed><!-- PROVISIONAL -->
      <MarketValue>900</MarketValue><!-- PROVISIONAL -->
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>5</ComfyTemperatureMin><!-- PROVISIONAL -->
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>55</ComfyTemperatureMax><!-- PROVISIONAL -->
      <FilthRate>30</FilthRate><!-- PROVISIONAL -->
      <Wildness>1</Wildness><!-- item §1 first value -->
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>head</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>28</power><!-- PROVISIONAL -->
        <cooldownTime>2.6</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>HeadAttackTool</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <ensureLinkedBodyPartsGroupAlwaysUsable>true</ensureLinkedBodyPartsGroupAlwaysUsable>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>left foot</label>
        <labelNoLocation>foot</labelNoLocation>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>22</power><!-- PROVISIONAL -->
        <cooldownTime>2.2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontLeftLeg</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>right foot</label>
        <labelNoLocation>foot</labelNoLocation>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>22</power><!-- PROVISIONAL -->
        <cooldownTime>2.2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontRightLeg</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <comps>
      <!-- Always holds RM_ThurrockShatter from spawn (built comp, see header). -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.CompProperties_GrantHediff">
        <hediff>RM_ThurrockShatter</hediff>
        <inspectLine>Fells trees as it browses.</inspectLine>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <race>
      <herdAnimal>true</herdAnimal>
      <!-- Vanilla hooved body with a hump (no new rig); the hump is the slab shoulder. -->
      <body>QuadrupedAnimalWithHoovesAndHump</body>
      <baseBodySize>8</baseBodySize><!-- item §1 -->
      <baseHealthScale>6</baseHealthScale><!-- PROVISIONAL -->
      <baseHungerRate>2.6</baseHungerRate><!-- PROVISIONAL -->
      <!-- Item §1: browses tree crowns (Tree) as well as plants. -->
      <foodType>VegetarianRoughAnimal, Tree</foodType>
      <leatherDef>Leather_Elephant</leatherDef>
      <trainability>None</trainability><!-- item §1 first value -->
      <predator>false</predator>
      <lifeExpectancy>60</lifeExpectancy><!-- PROVISIONAL -->
      <gestationPeriodDays>20</gestationPeriodDays><!-- PROVISIONAL -->
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>0.6</manhunterOnDamageChance><!-- PROVISIONAL -->
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.4</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.9</minAge>
          <soundWounded>Pawn_Elephant_Injured</soundWounded>
          <soundDeath>Pawn_Elephant_Dead</soundDeath>
          <soundCall>Pawn_Elephant_Call</soundCall>
          <soundAngry>Pawn_Elephant_Angry</soundAngry>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
      <soundEating>Herbivore_Eat</soundEating>
    </race>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalUncommon</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RM_Thurrock</defName>
    <label>thurrock</label>
    <race>RM_Thurrock</race>
    <combatPower>400</combatPower><!-- PROVISIONAL -->
    <ecoSystemWeight>2</ecoSystemWeight><!-- PROVISIONAL -->
    <wildGroupSize>3~6</wildGroupSize><!-- item §1 -->
